    {
      "chord_quality": "min7",
      "function_role": "ii-chord-in-major-ii-v-i",
      "narrative": "Heussenstamm prescribes the minor seventh chord as the naturally occurring ii in a major-key ii-V-I, and teaches chord-tone-only arpeggio improvisation through the 9th (e.g., Cm9) as the first melodic approach -- mapping chord members across the fretboard to develop harmonic ear before adding scales. Chapter 2, p. 9 and p. 14.",
