    {
      "chord_quality": "min7",
      "function_role": "dorian-scale-source",
      "narrative": "For improvisation on the ii min7 chord, Heussenstamm prescribes D Dorian as the obvious scale choice (modal sibling of G Mixolydian and C major), and teaches arpeggio construction by extracting the 1st, 3rd, 5th, and 7th of Dorian -- yielding root, 3rd, 5th, b7. He frames this as the scalar foundation before chord-tone exercises. Chapter 2, p. 9 and p. 14.",
