    },
    {
      "chord_quality": "maj7",
      "function_role": "i-chord-in-major-ii-v-i",
      "narrative": "Heussenstamm fixes maj7 as the I chord in a major-key ii-V-I, teaches C major scale over Cmaj7, and extends it to maj9 for chord-tone arpeggio exercises. The 7th-to-3rd voice-leading rule (each chord's 7th resolving to the next chord's 3rd) is the governing melodic principle at the I chord arrival. Chapter 2, p. 9.",
      "source_principle_ids": [],
      "source_work_id": "goldmine-100-jazz-lessons",
      "references": [
