    },
    {
      "chord_quality": "maj7",
      "function_role": "lydian-maj7-sharp-11-voicing",
      "narrative": "Heussenstamm teaches that the Lydian scale (major with raised 4th) generates the maj7#11 chord via stacked thirds, making Lydian the correct scale for improvising over maj7#11 -- and prescribes B minor pentatonic (C Lydian minus the tonic and 5th, which can sound dissonant against the chord) as a practical shortcut for soloing over Cmaj7#11. Chapter 6, p. 56-57.",
      "source_principle_ids": [],
