    {
      "chord_quality": "maj7",
      "function_role": "tonic-and-5th-avoid-over-maj7sharp11",
      "narrative": "Heussenstamm proscribes sustaining the tonic and 5th of C Lydian in a medium or high register over a Cmaj7#11 chord, because these tones can sound dissonant against parts of the chord -- recommending B minor pentatonic (which omits them) as the practical alternative. Chapter 6, p. 57.",
