    {
      "chord_quality": "maj7",
      "function_role": "half-step-outside-tritone-sub-device",
      "narrative": "Heussenstamm prescribes approaching a maj7 chord from a maj7 a half step above as an outside device, justified by tritone-substitution logic -- Dbmaj7 standing in for G7 (itself a tritone sub of Db dominant) resolves chromatically into Cmaj7, lending V-I mojo to what sounds like sliding one fret down. Chapter 7, p. 86.",
