    {
      "chord_quality": "dom7alt",
      "function_role": "v-chord-in-minor-ii-v-i",
      "narrative": "Heussenstamm prescribes an altered dominant (at minimum with a flatted or raised 9th) as the V chord in a minor ii-V-i, stating the tendency is 'strong' for V-i motion to use an altered dominant -- this is the strongest single prescriptive rule in the book for altered dominant choice. Super Locrian is the corresponding scale. Chapter 2, p. 10; Chapter 4, p. 31.",
