    {
      "chord_quality": "dom7alt",
      "function_role": "super-locrian-as-master-altered-scale",
      "narrative": "Heussenstamm prescribes super Locrian (seventh mode of melodic minor, built a half step above the altered dominant root) as the master scale capturing all four altered tones (b5, #5, b9, #9) plus root, 3rd, b7 -- forming a dom7 without the perfect 5th. G super Locrian = Ab melodic minor. Chapter 1, p. 6; Chapter 11, p. 160.",
